IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ohsr-dates`

-- Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 (Vic), S.R. No. 22/2017, Version No. 018 (20 October 2026) --
-- seat-neutral core.
--
-- The duties whose breach a person injured or made ill at work relies on: Part 2.1 (risk control measures, health
-- monitoring, confidentiality of reports), Part 3.1 (hazardous manual handling), Part 3.2 (noise), Part 3.3 (falls),
-- Part 3.4 (confined spaces), Part 3.5 (plant: the employer's duties and the prescribed plant for incident
-- notification), Part 4.1 (hazardous substances), Part 4.2 (scheduled carcinogenic substances), Part 4.3 (lead),
-- Part 4.4 (asbestos), Part 4.5 (crystalline silica), Part 5.1 (construction, with the notice of construction
-- excavation work), and the penalty of each provision in scope.
--
-- How a regulation is enforced (r 7): a provision with an "Act compliance" note sets out how a duty under that section
-- of the Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 is performed, so its breach is a breach of that section and carries the
-- section's penalty; a provision with its own penalty is an offence against the Regulations. The Act's penalties are
-- restated narrowly from the Act (Version No. 045), with the section, because a module cannot import across subjects.
--
-- Conventions (the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 rulings, NOTES.md): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own
-- words ("if", "unless", "means", "does not apply", a closed "except", a period the text fixes); NOTHING where it is
-- silent, a list is open, or a fact lies outside the deposit. "So far as is reasonably practicable", "reasonable grounds",
-- "as soon as reasonably possible", "adequately", a practitioner's opinion and the Authority's determinations are
-- inputs, never decided here. Penalties are in penalty units (the value of a penalty unit is not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 -- core`

§§ `To whom the employer's duties reach (r 8; Act s 21(3))`

-- r 8(1): a provision setting out how an employer complies with its s 21 or s 35 duty to employees extends to its duty
-- under that section to an independent contractor it engaged and the contractor's employees; r 8(2): where a provision
-- says the duty "extends to an independent contractor", it applies as if "employee" meant the contractor and its
-- employees, "in relation to matters over which the employer has control or would have control if not for any agreement
-- purporting to limit or remove that control". The Act's s 21(3)(b) sets the same limit for s 21.
-- JUST TRUE: an employee, or a contractor (or its employee) on a matter within the employer's control.
-- NOTHING: a contractor on a matter outside that control (a scope limit in the text's own words, no "only").
-- JUST FALSE: neither (the Regulations' employer duties speak of employees; a visitor's protection is s 23 of the Act).
GIVEN `is an employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an independent contractor the employer engaged, or an employee of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is within the employer's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer's duty reaches the person (r 8)` MEANS
    IF `is an employee of the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `is an independent contractor the employer engaged, or an employee of one`
         THEN IF `the matter is within the employer's control`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `The orders of control (rr 27, 34, 44, 56, 98, 163, 184, 238, 325)`

-- Each Part names the measures an employer must turn to, in order, once eliminating the risk is not reasonably
-- practicable. A measure further down may be relied on only if every measure above it is not reasonably practicable
-- ("If it is not reasonably practicable to ...", "If the employer has complied with subregulations (1) and (2) so far as is
-- reasonably practicable and a risk ... remains"). The measures one subregulation lists together (r 27(2)(a)-(d),
-- r 34(3)(a)-(c), r 98(2)(a)-(d), r 163(2)(a)-(d), r 184(2)(a)-(d), r 325(2)(a)-(d), r 44(5)(a)-(b)) share a rank.
DECLARE `Control measure` IS ONE OF
    `eliminating the risk`
    `altering the workplace layout, environment or system of work`
    `changing the things handled`
    `mechanical aids`
    `substitution`
    `isolation`
    `engineering controls`
    `a passive fall prevention device`
    `a work positioning system`
    `a fall arrest system`
    `a ladder`
    `administrative controls`
    `information, instruction or training`
    `personal protective equipment, including hearing protectors`
    `enclosing the asbestos`
    `sealing the asbestos`
    `other measures that take the listed matters into account`
    `no measure`

DECLARE `Hazard` IS ONE OF
    `hazardous manual handling (r 27)`
    `noise (r 34)`
    `a fall of more than 2 metres (r 44)`
    `work in a confined space (r 56)`
    `plant (r 98)`
    `a hazardous substance (r 163)`
    `lead (r 184)`
    `asbestos at the workplace (r 238)`
    `construction work (r 325)`

-- The rank of a measure in the order the Part sets; 99 for a measure the Part does not name.
GIVEN `the measure` IS A `Control measure`
      `the hazard`  IS A `Hazard`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank of` `the measure` `for` `the hazard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the measure`
    WHEN `eliminating the risk` THEN 1
    WHEN `no measure` THEN 99
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the hazard`
        WHEN `hazardous manual handling (r 27)` THEN
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `altering the workplace layout, environment or system of work` THEN 2
            WHEN `changing the things handled` THEN 2
            WHEN `mechanical aids` THEN 2
            WHEN `information, instruction or training` THEN 3
            OTHERWISE 99
        WHEN `noise (r 34)` THEN
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `substitution` THEN 2
            WHEN `engineering controls` THEN 2
            WHEN `administrative controls` THEN 3
            WHEN `personal protective equipment, including hearing protectors` THEN 4
            OTHERWISE 99
        WHEN `a fall of more than 2 metres (r 44)` THEN
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `a passive fall prevention device` THEN 2
            WHEN `a work positioning system` THEN 3
            WHEN `a fall arrest system` THEN 4
            WHEN `a ladder` THEN 5
            WHEN `administrative controls` THEN 5
            OTHERWISE 99
        WHEN `work in a confined space (r 56)` THEN
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `other measures that take the listed matters into account` THEN 2
            OTHERWISE 99
        WHEN `asbestos at the workplace (r 238)` THEN
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `enclosing the asbestos` THEN 2
            WHEN `sealing the asbestos` THEN 3
            OTHERWISE 99
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the measure`
            WHEN `substitution` THEN 2
            WHEN `isolation` THEN 2
            WHEN `engineering controls` THEN 2
            WHEN `administrative controls` THEN 3
            WHEN `personal protective equipment, including hearing protectors` THEN 4
            OTHERWISE 99

-- The control duty of each Part. Inputs: the highest-ranked measure the employer relied on; the highest-ranked
-- measure that was reasonably practicable (a judgment for the court); whether the risk was reduced so far as
-- reasonably practicable with the measures used (a judgment for the court).
-- JUST FALSE: the risk was eliminated, or the employer used a measure at least as high as the highest reasonably
-- practicable one and reduced the risk so far as reasonably practicable.
-- JUST TRUE: it relied on a lower measure than was reasonably practicable, used none, or did not reduce the risk so
-- far as reasonably practicable.
-- NOTHING: the measure said to be the highest reasonably practicable is not one the Part names.
GIVEN `the hazard` IS A `Hazard`
      `the measure relied on` IS A `Control measure`
      `the highest measure reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure`
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the control duty was contravened` MEANS
    IF `used rank` EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `best rank` EQUALS 99
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `used rank` GREATER THAN `best rank`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `used rank` MEANS `the rank of` `the measure relied on` `for` `the hazard`
        `best rank` MEANS `the rank of` `the highest measure reasonably practicable` `for` `the hazard`

-- When the employer must review, and if necessary revise, its controls (rr 28(1), 36(1), 48(1), 62(1), 164(1), 185(1),
-- 239(1), 326(1)). Each lists its occasions; "for any other reason, the risk control measures do not adequately control
-- the risks" is in every list. Plant's review provision (r 121) is not encoded: NOTHING for plant.
DECLARE `Review occasion` IS ONE OF
    `a change to the work, plant or system of work is about to be made`
    `new or additional information about the hazard has become available`
    `a musculoskeletal disorder was reported`
    `an audiological report found hearing loss likely due to noise`
    `health monitoring identified adverse health effects`
    `a worker was removed from lead-risk work`
    `an incident to which Part 5 of the Act applies happened`
    `the controls do not adequately control the risk`
    `a health and safety representative asked for a review`
    `none of these`

-- JUST TRUE: the occasion is one the Part lists. JUST FALSE: it is not (each list sets the occasions in its own words).
GIVEN `the hazard`   IS A `Hazard`
      `the occasion` IS A `Review occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the controls must be reviewed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the hazard`
    WHEN `plant (r 98)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the occasion`
        WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `the controls do not adequately control the risk` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a health and safety representative asked for a review` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an incident to which Part 5 of the Act applies happened` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `construction work (r 325)` THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a change to the work, plant or system of work is about to be made` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `work in a confined space (r 56)` THEN JUST FALSE
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `new or additional information about the hazard has become available` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `hazardous manual handling (r 27)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `construction work (r 325)` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        WHEN `a musculoskeletal disorder was reported` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `hazardous manual handling (r 27)` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        WHEN `an audiological report found hearing loss likely due to noise` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `noise (r 34)` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        WHEN `health monitoring identified adverse health effects` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `a hazardous substance (r 163)` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        WHEN `a worker was removed from lead-risk work` THEN
            CONSIDER `the hazard`
            WHEN `lead (r 184)` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2.1 -- general duties (rr 18-20)`

-- r 18(1): a person required by these Regulations to use a particular measure to control risk must ensure it is properly
-- installed (if applicable), used and maintained. r 18(2): "This regulation does not apply to a measure required by
-- Part 5.2 ... or Part 5.3".
GIVEN `the measure is required by these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is required by Part 5.2 or Part 5.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure was properly installed, used and maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 18 was contravened` MEANS
    IF `the measure is required by Part 5.2 or Part 5.3`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `the measure is required by these Regulations`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the measure was properly installed, used and maintained`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 19(1)-(3): "This regulation applies if, under these Regulations, an employer is required to ensure that an employee
-- is medically examined or that any other form of health monitoring is conducted"; the employer must tell the employee
-- its purpose and its type or nature, and it "is to be undertaken at the employer's expense".
GIVEN `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer must pay for the examination or monitoring (r 19(3))` MEANS
    IF `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer told the employee its purpose and nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee was charged for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 19 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the employer told the employee its purpose and nature`) OR `the employee was charged for it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 20(1): the report of a medical examination or health monitoring required by these Regulations, and any summary,
-- must be kept confidential "except in the circumstances set out in subregulation (2)": to the person it relates to
-- (as soon as reasonably possible after the employer receives it); to a third party the person authorised in writing;
-- to the Authority on request or where the Regulations require.
DECLARE `Report recipient` IS ONE OF
    `the person the report is about`
    `a third party the person authorised in writing`
    `the Authority, on request or where these Regulations require`
    `anyone else`

-- JUST TRUE: one of the r 20(2) recipients. JUST FALSE: anyone else (a closed "except").
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Report recipient`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the report may be disclosed to the recipient (r 20)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3.1 -- hazardous manual handling (rr 5, 26-28)`

-- r 5 "hazardous manual handling means work requiring the use of force exerted by a person to lift, lower, push, pull,
-- carry or otherwise move, hold or restrain" (a) a thing, if the work involves (i) repetitive or sustained application of
-- force, (ii) sustained awkward posture, (iii) repetitive movement, (iv) high force a person in the workforce may
-- reasonably be expected to have difficulty with, or (v) exposure to sustained vibration; (b) live persons or animals;
-- (c) unstable or unbalanced loads or loads that are difficult to grasp or hold.
GIVEN `the work requires force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves repetitive or sustained force, sustained awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is handled is a live person or animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the load is unstable, unbalanced or difficult to grasp or hold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is hazardous manual handling (r 5)` IF
        `the work requires force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something`
    AND (   `it involves repetitive or sustained force, sustained awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration`
         OR `what is handled is a live person or animal`
         OR `the load is unstable, unbalanced or difficult to grasp or hold`)

-- r 5 "musculoskeletal disorder means an injury, illness or disease that arises in whole or in part from hazardous manual
-- handling, whether occurring suddenly or over a prolonged period, but does not include an injury caused by crushing,
-- entrapment or cutting resulting primarily from the mechanical operation of plant".
GIVEN `the injury arose in whole or in part from hazardous manual handling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury was crushing, entrapment or cutting caused mainly by the mechanical operation of plant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the injury is a musculoskeletal disorder (r 5)` IF
        `the injury arose in whole or in part from hazardous manual handling`
    AND (NOT `the injury was crushing, entrapment or cutting caused mainly by the mechanical operation of plant`)

-- r 26: the employer must, so far as is reasonably practicable, identify any hazardous manual handling; r 27: the order of
-- control (above), with r 27(4): "only rely solely or primarily on the use of information, instruction or training ... if
-- none of the measures set out in subregulation (2) is reasonably practicable" (the rank does this).
-- JUST FALSE: the work is not hazardous manual handling (the Part's duties are about it; s 21 of the Act still applies).
-- JUST TRUE: not identified, or the order of control not followed.
GIVEN `the work is hazardous manual handling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer identified it so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure relied on` IS A `Control measure`
      `the highest measure reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure`
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 3.1 was contravened (rr 26, 27)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the work is hazardous manual handling`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `the employer identified it so far as reasonably practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE `the control duty was contravened` `hazardous manual handling (r 27)` `the measure relied on` `the highest measure reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

§§ `Part 3.2 -- noise (rr 5, 32-40)`

-- r 5 "noise exposure standard means (a) the 8 hour equivalent continuous sound pressure level of 85 decibels (A) ... at an
-- employee's ear position; or (b) the C-weighted peak hold sound pressure level reading of 140 decibels (C)". Exposure
-- "exceeds" the standard when it is above either figure; exactly 85 dB(A) or exactly 140 dB(C) does not.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 8-hour noise limit in dB(A)` MEANS 85

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the peak noise limit in dB(C)` MEANS 140

GIVEN `the 8-hour equivalent level in dB(A)` IS A NUMBER
      `the peak level in dB(C)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the noise exposure standard is exceeded (r 5)` IF
        `the 8-hour equivalent level in dB(A)` GREATER THAN `the 8-hour noise limit in dB(A)`
    OR  `the peak level in dB(C)` GREATER THAN `the peak noise limit in dB(C)`

-- r 32(1): the employer must determine an employee's exposure "if there is uncertainty (based on reasonable grounds) as
-- to whether the noise exposure standard is or may be exceeded"; r 32(2), (3)(b): hearing protectors are not taken
-- into account.
GIVEN `there is reasonable uncertainty whether the standard is or may be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer must determine the exposure (r 32)` MEANS
    IF `there is reasonable uncertainty whether the standard is or may be exceeded` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 34(1): "An employer must ensure that no employee at the workplace is exposed to noise that exceeds the noise exposure
-- standard"; (2)-(5) the order: eliminate the source; substitute quieter plant or processes, engineering controls;
-- administrative controls; hearing protectors "so that it does not exceed the noise exposure standard".
-- JUST TRUE if the exposure the employee still receives (with any hearing protectors worn) exceeds the standard, or the
-- order of control was not followed.
GIVEN `the exposure received, with any hearing protectors, exceeds the standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure relied on` IS A `Control measure`
      `the highest measure reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure`
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 34 was contravened` MEANS
    IF `the exposure received, with any hearing protectors, exceeds the standard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `the control duty was contravened` `noise (r 34)` `the measure relied on` `the highest measure reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

-- r 37: "If an employer is required under regulation 34(5) to provide hearing protectors to an employee, the employer must
-- provide for audiometric testing for that employee (a) within 3 months after the employee commences the work in relation
-- to which the hearing protectors are required; and (b) at any time when reasonably requested to do so by the health and
-- safety representative ...; and (c) at least every 2 years."
GIVEN `hearing protectors are required under r 34(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`audiometric testing is required (r 37)` MEANS
    IF `hearing protectors are required under r 34(5)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the day the work began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the first audiometric test (r 37(a))` MEANS `the date` 3 `months after` `the day the work began`

GIVEN `the day of the last test` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the next audiometric test (r 37(c))` MEANS `the date` 24 `months after` `the day of the last test`

-- r 38: "If the results of 2 or more audiometric tests of an employee under regulation 37 during a period not exceeding 2
-- years indicate a reduction in hearing levels equal to or greater than 15 decibels at 3000 hertz, 4000 hertz or 6000
-- hertz, the employer must provide for the employee to undergo an audiological examination as soon as reasonably
-- possible." Two tests compared; the later no more than 2 years after the earlier.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hearing reduction that triggers an audiological examination, in dB` MEANS 15

GIVEN `the reduction at 3000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction at 4000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction at 6000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the earlier test` IS A DATE
      `the day of the later test` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an audiological examination is required (r 38)` MEANS
    IF      `the day of the later test` `is on or before` (`the date` 24 `months after` `the day of the earlier test`)
        AND (   `the reduction at 3000 Hz in dB` AT LEAST `the hearing reduction that triggers an audiological examination, in dB`
             OR `the reduction at 4000 Hz in dB` AT LEAST `the hearing reduction that triggers an audiological examination, in dB`
             OR `the reduction at 6000 Hz in dB` AT LEAST `the hearing reduction that triggers an audiological examination, in dB`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 40(1): the employer "must keep the test results or examination report while the employee is employed by the
-- employer". JUST FALSE once the employment has ended ("while").
GIVEN `the employee is still employed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the audiometric results must still be kept (r 40(1))` MEANS
    IF `the employee is still employed by the employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3.3 -- prevention of falls (rr 5, 41, 44-46, 49)`

-- r 5 "fall, in Part 3.3 ..., means a person's involuntary fall of more than 2 metres". r 41(2): the Part does not apply
-- to (a) stunt work, acrobatics, a theatrical performance, sport, riding a bicycle, motorcycle or all-terrain vehicle,
-- horse riding, rock climbing or recreational abseiling under an employer's control; (b) a task on parts of a building or
-- structure that comply with AS 1657 and the Building Regulations 2006 and are used as designed; (c) an activity the
-- Authority has excluded under r 41(3).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fall height of Part 3.3, in metres` MEANS 2

GIVEN `the height of the possible fall in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `the activity is one r 41(2)(a) lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the task is on compliant building parts used as designed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has excluded the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 3.3 applies to the task (r 41)` MEANS
    IF `the height of the possible fall in metres` AT MOST `the fall height of Part 3.3, in metres`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the activity is one r 41(2)(a) lists` OR `the task is on compliant building parts used as designed` OR `the Authority has excluded the activity`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 44: eliminate the risk of a fall; then a passive fall prevention device; then a work positioning system; then a fall
-- arrest system; then a ladder (in accordance with r 45) or administrative controls. r 45: a ladder used to reduce the
-- risk must be fit for the purpose, appropriate for the duration of the task and set up correctly.
GIVEN `Part 3.3 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the measure relied on` IS A `Control measure`
      `the highest measure reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure`
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ladder used was fit for purpose, suited to the task's duration and set up correctly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 44 and 45 were contravened` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Part 3.3 applies`
    WHEN JUST `applies` THEN
        IF NOT `applies`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the measure relied on` EQUALS `a ladder` AND (NOT `a ladder used was fit for purpose, suited to the task's duration and set up correctly`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE `the control duty was contravened` `a fall of more than 2 metres (r 44)` `the measure relied on` `the highest measure reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- r 49(1): "If an employer uses a risk control measure in accordance with subregulation (2), (3), (4) or (5) of regulation
-- 44, the employer must ensure that emergency procedures are established ... before the task is undertaken" (rescue and
-- first aid, able to be carried out immediately after a fall).
GIVEN `the measure relied on` IS A `Control measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`fall emergency procedures are required before the task (r 49)` MEANS
    IF `rank` AT LEAST 2 AND `rank` AT MOST 5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `rank` EQUALS 1
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `rank` MEANS `the rank of` `the measure relied on` `for` `a fall of more than 2 metres (r 44)`

§§ `Part 3.4 -- confined spaces (rr 5, 50, 58, 60, 63-73)`

-- r 5 "safe oxygen level means an oxygen content in air under normal atmospheric pressure that (a) is equal to or greater
-- than 19.5% by volume ... but (b) is equal to or less than 23.5% by volume". The deposited text prints "195%" and "235%"
-- (and "198 kilopascals", "239 kilopascals"): the conversion lost the decimal points; 19.5% and 23.5% are the only
-- readings possible for a share of air (NOTES.md finding).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lowest safe oxygen level, per cent` MEANS 19.5

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest safe oxygen level, per cent` MEANS 23.5

GIVEN `the oxygen content in per cent by volume` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the atmosphere has a safe oxygen level (r 5)` IF
        `the oxygen content in per cent by volume` AT LEAST `the lowest safe oxygen level, per cent`
    AND `the oxygen content in per cent by volume` AT MOST `the highest safe oxygen level, per cent`

-- r 5 "confined space means a space in any vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, flue, oven, chimney, silo, reaction vessel,
-- container, receptacle, underground sewer or well, or any shaft, trench or tunnel or other similar enclosed or partially
-- enclosed structure, if the space (a) is, or is intended to be, or is likely to be, entered by any person; and (b) has a
-- limited or restricted means for entry or exit ...; and (c) is ... at normal atmospheric pressure while any person is in
-- the space; and (d) contains, or is intended to contain, or is likely to contain (i) ... a harmful level of any
-- contaminant; or (ii) an atmosphere that does not have a safe oxygen level; or (iii) any stored substance, except
-- liquids, that could cause engulfment -- but does not include a shaft, trench or tunnel that is a mine or is part of the
-- workings of a mine".
GIVEN `it is a vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, silo, sewer, well, shaft, trench, tunnel or similar enclosed structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person enters or is likely to enter it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its entry or exit is limited or restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at normal atmospheric pressure while someone is inside` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has or may have a harmful contaminant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has or may have an atmosphere without a safe oxygen level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has or may have a stored solid that could engulf a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a shaft, trench or tunnel of a mine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the space is a confined space (r 5)` IF
        `it is a vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, silo, sewer, well, shaft, trench, tunnel or similar enclosed structure`
    AND `a person enters or is likely to enter it`
    AND `its entry or exit is limited or restricted`
    AND `it is at normal atmospheric pressure while someone is inside`
    AND (   `it has or may have a harmful contaminant`
         OR `it has or may have an atmosphere without a safe oxygen level`
         OR `it has or may have a stored solid that could engulf a person`)
    AND (NOT `it is a shaft, trench or tunnel of a mine`)

-- r 60(1): (a) so far as reasonably practicable, any flammable gas or vapour must be below 5% of its lower explosive limit
-- (LEL); (b) if not, and it is (i) 5% or more but less than 10% of its LEL, "any employee is removed immediately from the
-- space unless a suitably-calibrated, continuous-monitoring, flammable gas detector is used in the space while the
-- employee is in the space"; or (ii) 10% or more of its LEL, any employee is removed immediately.
GIVEN `the flammable gas or vapour as a percentage of its LEL` IS A NUMBER
      `a calibrated continuous-monitoring flammable gas detector is in use in the space` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee must be removed from the space immediately (r 60)` MEANS
    IF `the flammable gas or vapour as a percentage of its LEL` AT LEAST 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the flammable gas or vapour as a percentage of its LEL` AT LEAST 5
         THEN IF `a calibrated continuous-monitoring flammable gas detector is in use in the space`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 50: the Part does not apply to an employer of an emergency service employee who, at the employer's direction, is
-- rescuing a person from, or giving first aid to a person in, a confined space. r 63(1): "An employer must ensure that an
-- employee does not enter a confined space unless the employer has issued a confined space entry permit ... permitting the
-- employee to enter"; (2)-(3): one space per permit; it lists the space, the controls, the name of each employee
-- permitted to enter, and the period it is in operation.
GIVEN `the employee entered the space` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a permit for this space named the employee and was in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an emergency service employee rescuing or giving first aid at the employer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 63 was contravened` MEANS
    IF `an emergency service employee rescuing or giving first aid at the employer's direction`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the employee entered the space` AND (NOT `a permit for this space named the employee and was in operation`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- rr 58(2)-(4), 65-67, 69-70, 73: during the work the atmosphere has a safe oxygen level or air-supplied respiratory
-- equipment is provided (r 58(2)); no exposure above an exposure standard, or respiratory equipment (r 58(3)); continuous
-- communication from outside and emergency procedures able to be started from outside (r 65); a procedure for knowing who
-- is inside (r 66); everyone out at the end (r 67); emergency procedures for rescue and first aid, rehearsed (r 69); air-
-- supplied respiratory equipment in an emergency from the atmosphere (r 70(1)); information, instruction and training
-- (r 73). JUST TRUE if any was failed.
GIVEN `the atmosphere was safe or air-supplied respiratory equipment was provided (r 58)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was continuous communication and emergency procedures could start from outside (r 65)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was a procedure for knowing who was inside and everyone was got out (rr 66, 67)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `emergency rescue and first aid procedures were in place and rehearsed (r 69)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee was given information, instruction and training (r 73)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an emergency service employee rescuing or giving first aid at the employer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the confined space working rules were contravened (rr 58, 65-67, 69, 73)` MEANS
    IF `an emergency service employee rescuing or giving first aid at the employer's direction`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `the atmosphere was safe or air-supplied respiratory equipment was provided (r 58)`
            AND `there was continuous communication and emergency procedures could start from outside (r 65)`
            AND `there was a procedure for knowing who was inside and everyone was got out (rr 66, 67)`
            AND `emergency rescue and first aid procedures were in place and rehearsed (r 69)`
            AND `the employee was given information, instruction and training (r 73)`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 64: the employer must keep each entry permit "(a) until the work to which it relates is completed; or (b) if a
-- notifiable incident occurs in connection with the work ..., for at least 2 years after the date on which the incident
-- occurs". "Notifiable incident" is defined neither here nor in the Act (NOTES.md finding); read as an incident the Act's
-- s 38 requires to be notified.
GIVEN `the day the work was completed` IS A DATE
      `a notifiable incident occurred in connection with the work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the entry permit must be kept until (r 64)` MEANS
    IF `a notifiable incident occurred in connection with the work`
    THEN `the date` 24 `months after` `the day of the incident`
    ELSE `the day the work was completed`

§§ `Part 3.5 -- plant (rr 74, 98, 99, 124)`

-- r 74(1): the Part applies to (a) plant that processes material by a mechanical action (cutting, drilling, punching,
-- grinding, pressing, forming, hammering, joining, moulding, combining, mixing, sorting, packaging, assembling, knitting,
-- weaving); (b) plant that lifts or moves persons or materials (not a ship, boat, aircraft, or a road or rail vehicle);
-- (c) pressure equipment; (d) tractors; (e) earthmoving machinery; (f) lasers; (g) scaffolds; (h) temporary access
-- equipment; (i) explosive-powered tools; (j) turbines; (k) amusement structures. r 74(2): (a) and (b) "do not include
-- plant that (a) relies exclusively on manual power for its operation; or (b) is designed to be primarily supported by
-- hand". r 74(4): Division 5 applies to a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace other than a public road or rail.
DECLARE `Plant kind` IS ONE OF
    `plant that processes material by mechanical action (r 74(1)(a))`
    `plant that lifts or moves persons or materials (r 74(1)(b))`
    `pressure equipment`
    `a tractor`
    `earthmoving machinery`
    `a laser`
    `a scaffold`
    `temporary access equipment`
    `an explosive-powered tool`
    `a turbine`
    `an amusement structure`
    `a ship, boat or aircraft`
    `a road or rail vehicle on a public road or rail`
    `a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace off public roads and rail`
    `other plant`

-- JUST TRUE: a kind r 74(1) lists. JUST FALSE: manual or hand-supported plant of kind (a) or (b), or a kind (b) excludes.
-- NOTHING: other plant (an open "applies to the following"; s 21 of the Act still applies to it).
GIVEN `the kind of plant` IS A `Plant kind`
      `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 3.5 applies to the plant (r 74)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of plant`
    WHEN `plant that processes material by mechanical action (r 74(1)(a))` THEN
        IF `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `plant that lifts or moves persons or materials (r 74(1)(b))` THEN
        IF `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace off public roads and rail` THEN
        IF `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a ship, boat or aircraft` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a road or rail vehicle on a public road or rail` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `other plant` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- r 124: "For the purposes of section 37(2)(e)(i) of the Act, plant referred to in regulation 74(1)(b), (c), (d), (e),
-- (g), (h), (i), (j) and (k) is prescribed." Under s 37(2)(e)(i) an incident involving the collapse, overturning,
-- failure or malfunction of, or damage to, prescribed plant is one the Act requires to be notified (Act baseline).
-- JUST TRUE: one of those kinds. JUST FALSE: any other (the Regulations close the list the Act hands to them).
GIVEN `the kind of plant` IS A `Plant kind`
      `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the plant is prescribed for incident notification (r 124)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of plant`
    WHEN `plant that processes material by mechanical action (r 74(1)(a))` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a laser` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a ship, boat or aircraft` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a road or rail vehicle on a public road or rail` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace off public roads and rail` THEN
        IF `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `other plant` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `plant that lifts or moves persons or materials (r 74(1)(b))` THEN
        IF `it relies only on manual power or is hand-supported` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- r 99(3): where guarding is used, it must be (a) a permanently fixed physical barrier if access to the guarded area is
-- not necessary during operation, maintenance or cleaning; (b) an interlocked physical barrier if access is necessary;
-- (c) if (a) or (b) is not reasonably practicable, a barrier that can only be altered or removed with tools; (d) if none
-- of those is reasonably practicable, a presence-sensing safeguarding system. r 99(1): the regulation applies only to an
-- employer that uses guarding.
DECLARE `Guarding kind` IS ONE OF
    `a permanently fixed physical barrier`
    `an interlocked physical barrier`
    `a physical barrier removable only with tools`
    `a presence-sensing safeguarding system`
    `no guarding`

GIVEN `the guarding` IS A `Guarding kind`
      `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank of the guarding (r 99(3))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the guarding`
    WHEN `a permanently fixed physical barrier` THEN
        IF `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning` THEN 99 ELSE 1
    WHEN `an interlocked physical barrier` THEN
        IF `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning` THEN 1 ELSE 99
    WHEN `a physical barrier removable only with tools` THEN 2
    WHEN `a presence-sensing safeguarding system` THEN 3
    WHEN `no guarding` THEN 99

GIVEN `the guarding used` IS A `Guarding kind`
      `the highest guarding reasonably practicable` IS A `Guarding kind`
      `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 99(3) was contravened` MEANS
    IF `the guarding used` EQUALS `no guarding`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `best` EQUALS 99
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `used` GREATER THAN `best` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `used` MEANS `the rank of the guarding (r 99(3))` `the guarding used` `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning`
        `best` MEANS `the rank of the guarding (r 99(3))` `the highest guarding reasonably practicable` `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning`

§§ `Records kept for 30 years (rr 168, 171, 175, 204, 263, 283, 313)`

-- rr 168(1), 171(1), 204, 263(2), 283(2), 313(2): the employer keeps the record "for (a) a period (not exceeding 30 years)
-- that is determined by the Authority; or (b) 30 years, if no period has been determined by the Authority". None says
-- from when; read from the day the record or report came into existence (NOTES.md finding). r 175(3) does say: "for 30
-- years from the date on which the person last worked with a scheduled carcinogenic substance at the employer's
-- workplace".
GIVEN `the day the record was made` IS A DATE
      `the Authority has determined a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period the Authority determined, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the record must be kept until` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has determined a period`
    THEN `the date` ((`the lesser of` `the period the Authority determined, in years` `and` 30) TIMES 12) `months after` `the day the record was made`
    ELSE `the date` 360 `months after` `the day the record was made`

GIVEN `the day the person last worked with the substance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the carcinogen work record must be kept until (r 175(3))` MEANS `the date` 360 `months after` `the day the person last worked with the substance`

§§ `Part 4.1 -- hazardous substances (rr 154, 163, 165, 166, 169)`

-- Schedule 9, Table 1 (hazardous substances other than lead requiring health monitoring) and Table 2 (lead).
DECLARE `Substance` IS ONE OF
    `acrylonitrile`
    `arsenic (inorganic)`
    `benzene`
    `cadmium`
    `chromium (inorganic)`
    `creosote`
    `crystalline silica`
    `isocyanates`
    `mercury (inorganic)`
    `MOCA (4,4'-methylene bis (2-chloroaniline))`
    `organophosphate pesticides`
    `pentachlorophenol (PCP)`
    `polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAH)`
    `thallium`
    `vinyl chloride`
    `lead`
    `another hazardous substance`

-- r 169(1): "An employer must ensure that health monitoring is carried out for an employee if (a) the employee is exposed
-- to any hazardous substance (i) listed in column 2 of Tables 1 or 2 of Schedule 9; or (ii) determined by the Authority to
-- be a hazardous substance for which health monitoring is required; and (b) the exposure ... is reasonably likely to have
-- an adverse effect on the employee's health under the particular conditions of work". r 154(2): the Subdivision does not
-- apply to lead in a lead process under Part 4.3 (Part 4.3 then governs the monitoring).
GIVEN `the substance` IS A `Substance`
      `the Authority has determined health monitoring is required for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exposure is reasonably likely to harm the employee's health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is a lead process (r 178)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`health monitoring is required (r 169)` MEANS
    IF `the substance` EQUALS `lead` AND `the work is a lead process (r 178)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF ((NOT (`the substance` EQUALS `another hazardous substance`)) OR `the Authority has determined health monitoring is required for it`)
            AND `the exposure is reasonably likely to harm the employee's health`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 165: "An employer must ensure that an employee is not exposed to an atmospheric concentration of a hazardous substance
-- supplied to or generated at the workplace above the exposure standard (if any) for the substance or any of its
-- ingredients." The exposure standards (Safe Work Australia's Workplace Exposure Standards for Airborne Contaminants) are
-- not deposited, so the figure is an input.
GIVEN `there is an exposure standard for the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exposure standard` IS A NUMBER
      `the concentration the employee was exposed to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 165 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is an exposure standard for the substance`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the concentration the employee was exposed to` GREATER THAN `the exposure standard`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 166: atmospheric monitoring must be carried out if there is an exposure standard and (a) there is uncertainty (on
-- reasonable grounds) whether it is or may be exceeded, or (b) monitoring is necessary to determine whether there is a
-- risk to health; r 166(2): not if health monitoring including biological monitoring is required under r 169.
GIVEN `there is an exposure standard for the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is reasonable uncertainty whether it is or may be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `monitoring is needed to tell whether there is a risk to health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `r 169 health monitoring with biological monitoring is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`atmospheric monitoring is required (r 166)` MEANS
    IF `r 169 health monitoring with biological monitoring is required`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `there is an exposure standard for the substance`
            AND (`there is reasonable uncertainty whether it is or may be exceeded` OR `monitoring is needed to tell whether there is a risk to health`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4.2 -- scheduled carcinogenic substances (rr 174-176)`

DECLARE `Carcinogen class` IS ONE OF
    `a Schedule 10 prohibited carcinogenic substance`
    `a Schedule 11 restricted carcinogenic substance`
    `not a scheduled carcinogenic substance`

-- r 174(1): no work with a Schedule 10 substance "unless (a) the workplace is a laboratory; and (b) the person (i) holds a
-- licence to use [it] at that laboratory ... or (ii) is an employee of a holder of such a licence"; (2)-(3): no work with a
-- Schedule 11 substance unless the person holds a licence for that laboratory or workplace, or is an employee of a holder.
-- JUST TRUE: the work is permitted. JUST FALSE: it is not ("unless"). NOTHING: not a scheduled substance.
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Carcinogen class`
      `the workplace is a laboratory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or their employer holds a carcinogens licence for this substance at this workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the work with the carcinogen is permitted (r 174)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a Schedule 10 prohibited carcinogenic substance` THEN
        IF `the workplace is a laboratory` AND `the person or their employer holds a carcinogens licence for this substance at this workplace`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a Schedule 11 restricted carcinogenic substance` THEN
        IF `the person or their employer holds a carcinogens licence for this substance at this workplace`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `not a scheduled carcinogenic substance` THEN NOTHING

-- r 176: "This regulation applies if a person has worked with a scheduled carcinogenic substance at an employer's
-- workplace"; the employer must give a written statement "when the person ceases to work at the workplace" (the
-- substances, the period, where the r 175 records are, and advice to have periodical health assessments).
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Carcinogen class`
      `the person has ceased to work at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a written statement of carcinogen work is due (r 176)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `not a scheduled carcinogenic substance` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the person has ceased to work at the workplace` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4.3 -- lead (rr 179, 186, 193-201)`

-- r 179: "a female employee engaged in a lead process is to be treated as being of reproductive capacity, unless she
-- provides her employer with a written statement advising the contrary".
GIVEN `the employee is female` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she has given the employer a written statement that she is not of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is treated as a woman of reproductive capacity (r 179)` IF
        `the employee is female`
    AND (NOT `she has given the employer a written statement that she is not of reproductive capacity`)

-- The lead figures changed on the 2-year anniversary of S.R. No. 71/2018 (5 June 2020): rr 186(1A), 193(2), 198(1A),
-- 199(1A), 200(3), 201(3A) apply "on and from" that day; the earlier figures before it.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day` IF
    `the 2-year anniversary of S.R. No. 71/2018` `is on or before` `the day`

-- r 186(1): 0.15 mg/m3 (8-hour, 40-hour-week time weighted average in the breathing zone); r 186(1A): 0.05 mg/m3 from
-- 5 June 2020. "exceeds".
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lead exposure standard in mg per cubic metre (r 186)` MEANS
    IF `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day` THEN 0.05 ELSE 0.15

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the airborne lead concentration in mg per cubic metre` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lead exposure standard is exceeded (r 186)` IF
    `the airborne lead concentration in mg per cubic metre` GREATER THAN `the lead exposure standard in mg per cubic metre (r 186)` `the day`

-- r 193: lead-risk work is work in a lead process reasonably likely to cause the blood lead level to exceed, for a woman
-- of reproductive capacity, 10 ug/dL (from 5 June 2020: 5), and otherwise 30 ug/dL (from 5 June 2020: 20). The text gives
-- each figure in umol/L too (0.48, 1.45; 0.24, 0.97); those are not exact conversions of the ug/dL figures (NOTES.md
-- finding). This encoding works in ug/dL.
GIVEN `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lead-risk blood lead level in ug per dL (r 193)` MEANS
    IF `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day`
    THEN IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 5 ELSE 20
    ELSE IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 10 ELSE 30

-- r 194(1): the employer must identify each lead process as either reasonably likely, or not reasonably likely, to cause
-- blood lead levels above the r 193 figures; r 194(4): "If an employer is unable to identify whether or not a lead process
-- is [one or the other], the process is to be treated as being reasonably likely to cause blood lead levels ... to exceed
-- those set out in regulation 193 until the employer establishes otherwise."
DECLARE `Lead identification` IS ONE OF
    `identified as reasonably likely to exceed the r 193 level`
    `identified as not reasonably likely to exceed the r 193 level`
    `not identified either way`

GIVEN `the work is a lead process (r 178)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identification` IS A `Lead identification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the work is lead-risk work (rr 193, 194)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the work is a lead process (r 178)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the identification`
         WHEN `identified as not reasonably likely to exceed the r 193 level` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- r 196(1): a medical examination and biological monitoring "before the employee first starts lead-risk work"; r 196(2):
-- biological monitoring "within one month after the employee starts lead-risk work".
-- JUST TRUE: either duty broken. JUST FALSE: both met. NOTHING: the month after starting is still running and there has
-- been no monitoring yet.
GIVEN `a medical examination and biological monitoring were done before starting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `biological monitoring was done after starting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day lead-risk work started` IS A DATE
      `the day of that monitoring` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 196 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `a medical examination and biological monitoring were done before starting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `biological monitoring was done after starting`
         THEN IF `the day of that monitoring` `is on or before` `the last day`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` `the last day`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the date` 1 `months after` `the day lead-risk work started`

-- r 198(1) (before 5 June 2020) and (1A) (from that day): the next biological monitoring falls due a fixed time after the
-- last, set by its result. A man, or a woman not of reproductive capacity: under 30 ug/dL 6 months, 30 to under 40 3
-- months, 40 or more 6 weeks (from 5 June 2020: under 10, 10 to under 20, 20 or more). A woman of reproductive capacity:
-- under 10 3 months, 10 or more 6 weeks (from 5 June 2020: under 5 3 months, 5 to under 10 6 weeks). r 198(1A)(b) sets no
-- interval for a woman of reproductive capacity at 10 ug/dL or more, who must instead be removed (r 199(1A)): NOTHING.
-- The figures in force on the day of the last monitoring are used (NOTES.md fork).
GIVEN `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the last monitoring` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the next biological monitoring is due by (r 198)` MEANS
    IF `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day of the last monitoring`
    THEN IF `of reproductive capacity`
         THEN IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 5
              THEN JUST `three months on`
              ELSE IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 10
                   THEN JUST `six weeks on`
                   ELSE NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 10
              THEN JUST `six months on`
              ELSE IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 20
                   THEN JUST `three months on`
                   ELSE JUST `six weeks on`
    ELSE IF `of reproductive capacity`
         THEN IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 10
              THEN JUST `three months on`
              ELSE JUST `six weeks on`
         ELSE IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 30
              THEN JUST `six months on`
              ELSE IF `the last blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN 40
                   THEN JUST `three months on`
                   ELSE JUST `six weeks on`
    WHERE
        `six months on`   MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the last monitoring`
        `three months on` MEANS `the date` 3 `months after` `the day of the last monitoring`
        `six weeks on`    MEANS `the date` 42 `days after` `the day of the last monitoring`

-- r 199(1) (before 5 June 2020): remove immediately if the blood lead level is "at or exceeding" 50 ug/dL (a man or a
-- woman not of reproductive capacity), 20 (a woman of reproductive capacity), 15 (a woman who is pregnant or
-- breastfeeding); r 199(1A) (from that day): 30 and 10, with no separate figure for pregnancy or breastfeeding. Also (b)
-- a registered medical practitioner's opinion that the employee must be removed, and (c) an indication that controls have
-- failed so that the level is likely to reach the figure. "must immediately remove ... if": JUST FALSE when none holds.
GIVEN `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pregnant or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the removal blood lead level in ug per dL (r 199)` MEANS
    IF `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day`
    THEN IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 10 ELSE 30
    ELSE IF `pregnant or breastfeeding`
         THEN 15
         ELSE IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 20 ELSE 50

GIVEN `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pregnant or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the result` IS A DATE
      `a medical practitioner is of the opinion the employee must be removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `controls have failed so the removal level is likely to be reached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee must be removed from lead-risk work (r 199)` MEANS
    IF     `the blood lead level in ug per dL` AT LEAST (`the removal blood lead level in ug per dL (r 199)` `of reproductive capacity` `pregnant or breastfeeding` `the day of the result`)
        OR `a medical practitioner is of the opinion the employee must be removed`
        OR `controls have failed so the removal level is likely to be reached`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Removal ground` IS ONE OF
    `the blood lead level reached the removal level (r 199(1)(a))`
    `a medical practitioner's opinion (r 199(1)(b))`
    `controls failed (r 199(1)(c))`

-- r 201(3) (before 5 June 2020) and (3A) (from that day): after removal on ground (a) or (b) the employer "must ensure
-- that the employee does not return to lead-risk work until (a) the employee's blood lead level is less than" 40 ug/dL (a
-- man or a woman not of reproductive capacity) or 10 (a woman of reproductive capacity) -- from 5 June 2020, 20 or 5 --
-- "and (b) a registered medical practitioner certifies that the employee is fit to return". r 200(2), (3): after removal
-- on ground (c), the employer "may allow the employee to return" if a medical examination shows the level is below the
-- r 199 removal figure and the practitioner agrees.
-- The "until" bar (ruling (d)): JUST TRUE while the employee must be kept off; JUST FALSE once the conditions are met
-- (the bar lifts; nothing says the employee must go back).
GIVEN `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the return blood lead level in ug per dL (r 201)` MEANS
    IF `the 2020 lead figures apply on` `the day`
    THEN IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 5 ELSE 20
    ELSE IF `of reproductive capacity` THEN 10 ELSE 40

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Removal ground`
      `of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pregnant or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the current blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the result` IS A DATE
      `a medical practitioner certifies or agrees the employee is fit to return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee must be kept off lead-risk work (rr 200, 201)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `controls failed (r 199(1)(c))` THEN
        IF     `the current blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN (`the removal blood lead level in ug per dL (r 199)` `of reproductive capacity` `pregnant or breastfeeding` `the day of the result`)
           AND `a medical practitioner certifies or agrees the employee is fit to return`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF     `the current blood lead level in ug per dL` LESS THAN (`the return blood lead level in ug per dL (r 201)` `of reproductive capacity` `the day of the result`)
           AND `a medical practitioner certifies or agrees the employee is fit to return`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 4.4 -- asbestos (rr 5, 210, 216, 225, 237, 262, 282, 298, 311)`

-- r 5 "asbestos exposure standard means 0.1 f/ml of air measured in a person's breathing zone and expressed as a time
-- weighted average fibre concentration ... over an 8 hour working day". r 216(2): 0.01 f/ml; rr 216(3), 262, 311: one
-- half of the standard.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the asbestos exposure standard in fibres per ml` MEANS 0.1

GIVEN `the fibre concentration in fibres per ml` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the asbestos exposure standard is exceeded (r 210)` IF
    `the fibre concentration in fibres per ml` GREATER THAN `the asbestos exposure standard in fibres per ml`

-- r 210: the employer or self-employed person must ensure no person is exposed above the asbestos exposure standard from
-- its undertaking, and must eliminate exposure to airborne asbestos fibres so far as reasonably practicable, or else
-- reduce it so far as reasonably practicable.
GIVEN `the fibre concentration in fibres per ml` IS A NUMBER
      `exposure was eliminated or reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 210 was contravened` MEANS
    IF `the asbestos exposure standard is exceeded (r 210)` `the fibre concentration in fibres per ml`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `exposure was eliminated or reduced so far as reasonably practicable` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 216(1): a broom, a brush (except for sealing), or a high pressure water jet, power tool or similar must not be used on
-- asbestos "unless the use is controlled"; (2): not if airborne fibre levels are not above 0.01 f/ml during use; (3):
-- controlled means enclosed or engineering controls so that a person is not likely to be exposed to more than one half of
-- the standard; (4): respiratory protective equipment cannot be relied on for that.
GIVEN `such a tool was used on asbestos` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fibre level during use in fibres per ml` IS A NUMBER
      `the tool was enclosed or engineering controls kept likely exposure to half the standard, without relying on respirators` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 216 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `such a tool was used on asbestos`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the fibre level during use in fibres per ml` AT MOST 0.01
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the tool was enclosed or engineering controls kept likely exposure to half the standard, without relying on respirators`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 225(1): Division 5 "applies to a workplace where asbestos is present in a building, structure, ship or plant or has
-- been identified elsewhere at the workplace"; (2): "does not apply to a domestic premises that is a workplace only because
-- of work being performed by an employer or self-employed person engaged to perform the work". r 237(a): the employer
-- must ensure a copy of the employer's asbestos register is readily accessible to any employee.
GIVEN `asbestos is present or has been identified at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the workplace is a home that is a workplace only because a business is working there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employee may see the employer's asbestos register (r 237)` MEANS
    IF `the workplace is a home that is a workplace only because a business is working there`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `asbestos is present or has been identified at the workplace`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the person is an employee of the employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Asbestos work` IS ONE OF
    `limited asbestos removal work (r 262)`
    `licensed asbestos removal work (r 282)`
    `asbestos-related activities (r 311)`

-- rr 262(1), 311(1): medical examinations for each employee in ongoing work "if there is a risk of exposure to airborne
-- asbestos fibres in excess of one half of the asbestos exposure standard" (respirators not taken into account); r 282(1):
-- for each person engaged in licensed asbestos removal work, without that condition.
GIVEN `the work` IS AN `Asbestos work`
      `the work is ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`asbestos medical examinations are required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the work`
    WHEN `licensed asbestos removal work (r 282)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the work is ongoing` AND `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Before starting: r 262(3)(a) "before the employee commences asbestos removal work for the first time for that employer
-- unless the employee has had an appropriate medical examination within the preceding 2 years"; r 282(2)(a) the same with
-- "within the preceding year". r 311 sets no examination before starting: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the work` IS AN `Asbestos work`
      `examinations are required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has had an earlier examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the earlier examination` IS A DATE
      `the day the work starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an asbestos examination is required before starting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `examinations are required`
    WHEN JUST `required` THEN
        IF NOT `required`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE CONSIDER `the work`
             WHEN `asbestos-related activities (r 311)` THEN NOTHING
             WHEN `limited asbestos removal work (r 262)` THEN `unless within` 24
             WHEN `licensed asbestos removal work (r 282)` THEN `unless within` 12
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `unless within` `months` MEANS
            IF `the person has had an earlier examination` AND `the day the work starts` `is on or before` (`the date` `months` `months after` `the day of the earlier examination`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- After ceasing: rr 262(3)(c), 282(2)(c), 311(4)(b): "within 30 days after the [person] has ceased ... unless the
-- [person] has had an appropriate medical examination within the preceding year".
GIVEN `examinations are required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has had an earlier examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the earlier examination` IS A DATE
      `the day the work ceased` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an asbestos examination is required after ceasing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `examinations are required`
    WHEN JUST `required` THEN
        IF NOT `required`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the person has had an earlier examination` AND `the day the work ceased` `is on or before` (`the date` 12 `months after` `the day of the earlier examination`)
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the day the work ceased` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the examination after ceasing` MEANS `the date` 30 `days after` `the day the work ceased`

-- rr 262(3)(b), 282(2)(b), 311(4)(a): "at intervals of not more than 2 years".
GIVEN `the day of the last examination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the next asbestos examination` MEANS `the date` 24 `months after` `the day of the last examination`

-- r 298(1): the asbestos removal licence holder must notify the Authority "(a) if the work involves removal of a total
-- area of 10 square metres or less of non-friable asbestos-containing material ..., at least 24 hours before the work
-- commences; or (b) in any other case, at least 5 days before the work commences". Measured in hours; 5 days read as 120
-- hours (NOTES.md fork).
GIVEN `the area to be removed in square metres` IS A NUMBER
      `the material is friable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours of notice required (r 298)` MEANS
    IF `the area to be removed in square metres` AT MOST 10 AND (NOT `the material is friable`)
    THEN 24
    ELSE 120

§§ `Part 4.5 -- crystalline silica (rr 5, 319C, 319L, 319S, 319V, 319Y-319ZB)`

-- r 5 "engineered stone means an artificial product that (a) contains 1% or more crystalline silica, determined as a
-- weight/weight (w/w) concentration; and (b) is created by combining natural stone materials with other chemical
-- constituents such as water, resins or pigments; and (c) becomes hardened; and (d) is not" concrete or cement, brick,
-- paver or block, ceramic tile, porcelain or sintered stone without resin, roof tile, grout, mortar or render,
-- plasterboard, or a product the Authority has determined is not engineered stone.
GIVEN `the crystalline silica content in per cent w/w` IS A NUMBER
      `it combines natural stone with other constituents such as water, resins or pigments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it becomes hardened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is one of the excluded products` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the product is engineered stone (r 5)` IF
        `the crystalline silica content in per cent w/w` AT LEAST 1
    AND `it combines natural stone with other constituents such as water, resins or pigments`
    AND `it becomes hardened`
    AND (NOT `it is one of the excluded products`)

-- r 319C: "High risk crystalline silica work is (a) an engineered stone process; or (b) work performed in connection with
-- a crystalline silica process that is reasonably likely to result in (i) an airborne concentration of respirable
-- crystalline silica that exceeds half the exposure standard ...; or (ii) a risk to the health of a person"; r 319J(4): if
-- the employer cannot identify whether it is, it is treated as high risk until it can.
GIVEN `the work is an engineered stone process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is a crystalline silica process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has not been able to identify whether it is high risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is high risk crystalline silica work (rr 319C, 319J(4))` IF
        `the work is an engineered stone process`
    OR  (    `the work is a crystalline silica process`
         AND (`it is reasonably likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` OR `the employer has not been able to identify whether it is high risk`))

-- r 319L(1): no high risk crystalline silica work "unless (a) a crystalline silica hazard control statement is prepared for
-- the work before the work commences; and (b) the work is performed in accordance with that statement"; (3): for high risk
-- construction work, a safe work method statement covering the same matters suffices.
GIVEN `the work is high risk crystalline silica work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a hazard control statement (or a safe work method statement covering it) was prepared before the work began` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work was done in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 319L was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `the work is high risk crystalline silica work`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a hazard control statement (or a safe work method statement covering it) was prepared before the work began` AND `the work was done in accordance with it`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 319S(1): a power tool or mechanical plant used for an engineered stone process must be used with (a) an integrated
-- water delivery system, or (b) commercially available on-tool dust extraction connected to a Dust Class H vacuum or another
-- capture system, or (c) if neither is reasonably practicable, local exhaust ventilation. r 319V: the employer must provide
-- respiratory protective equipment to an employee who undertakes an engineered stone process, and ensure it is used.
DECLARE `Dust control` IS ONE OF
    `an integrated water delivery system`
    `on-tool dust extraction to a Class H vacuum or capture system`
    `local exhaust ventilation`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the work is an engineered stone process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a power tool or mechanical plant was used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dust control used` IS A `Dust control`
      `water delivery or on-tool extraction was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `respiratory protective equipment was provided and its use ensured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 319S and 319V were contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `the work is an engineered stone process`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `respiratory protective equipment was provided and its use ensured`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF NOT `a power tool or mechanical plant was used`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE CONSIDER `the dust control used`
                   WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN `local exhaust ventilation` THEN
                        IF `water delivery or on-tool extraction was reasonably practicable` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
                   OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- r 319Y: an employer, a self-employed person or a person managing or controlling a workplace "must not carry out, or
-- direct or allow a person ... to do, any of the following (a) install, manufacture, or supply engineered stone benchtops,
-- panels or slabs; (b) perform an engineered stone process involving benchtops, panels or slabs". Exceptions: r 319Z
-- installation for research or analysis or to sample or identify; r 319ZA supply for those or to dispose; r 319ZB
-- processing for those, to remove, repair or modify engineered stone already installed, or to dispose, "and" carried out
-- in accordance with Subdivision 3 of Division 3 (rr 319S-319X). The present r 319Y was substituted by S.R. No. 63/2024
-- from 1 July 2024; the earlier text is not deposited: NOTHING before that day.
DECLARE `Engineered stone activity` IS ONE OF
    `installing`
    `manufacturing`
    `supplying`
    `processing (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like)`

DECLARE `Engineered stone purpose` IS ONE OF
    `research or analysis`
    `sampling or identifying engineered stone`
    `removing, repairing or modifying engineered stone already installed`
    `disposing of engineered stone`
    `ordinary work`

-- JUST TRUE: prohibited. JUST FALSE: an exception applies. NOTHING: before 1 July 2024, or not a benchtop, panel or slab
-- (r 319Y is limited to those in its own words).
GIVEN `the day of the work` IS A DATE
      `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity` IS AN `Engineered stone activity`
      `the purpose` IS AN `Engineered stone purpose`
      `the processing complies with rr 319S-319X` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the engineered stone work is prohibited (r 319Y)` MEANS
    IF `the day of the work` `is before` `the engineered stone prohibition day` OR (NOT `it is a benchtop, panel or slab`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the activity`
         WHEN `manufacturing` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `installing` THEN
             CONSIDER `the purpose`
             WHEN `research or analysis` THEN JUST FALSE
             WHEN `sampling or identifying engineered stone` THEN JUST FALSE
             OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
         WHEN `supplying` THEN
             CONSIDER `the purpose`
             WHEN `research or analysis` THEN JUST FALSE
             WHEN `sampling or identifying engineered stone` THEN JUST FALSE
             WHEN `disposing of engineered stone` THEN JUST FALSE
             OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
         WHEN `processing (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like)` THEN
             CONSIDER `the purpose`
             WHEN `ordinary work` THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE IF `the processing complies with rr 319S-319X` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 5.1 -- construction (rr 321, 322, 327, 332, 341, 342, 349, 354, 558)`

-- r 321(1): "construction work means any work performed in connection with the construction, alteration, conversion,
-- fitting out, commissioning, renovation, refurbishment, decommissioning, or demolition of any building or structure, or any
-- similar activity", with the work in (2)(a)-(g); r 321(3): it "does not include" assembling or making fixed plant,
-- prefabrication away from a place set up for the project, routine or minor testing, maintenance or repair, or exploring
-- for or extracting minerals or stone.
GIVEN `the work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is one r 321(3) excludes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is construction work (r 321)` IF
        `the work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure`
    AND (NOT `the work is one r 321(3) excludes`)

-- r 322: high risk construction work is construction work (a) "where there is a risk of a person falling more than 2
-- metres", (g) "involving a trench or shaft if the excavated depth is more than 1.5 metres", or any of (b)-(f), (h)-(s)
-- (telecommunications towers, demolition, asbestos, temporary structural support, confined spaces, tunnels, explosives,
-- gas mains, chemical, fuel or refrigerant lines, energised electrical installations, contaminated or flammable
-- atmospheres, tilt-up or precast concrete, roads and railways in use, powered mobile plant, artificial extremes of
-- temperature, water with a risk of drowning, diving). "means": JUST FALSE when none.
GIVEN `the work is construction work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the height a person could fall, in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `the depth of any trench or shaft, in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `the work has another of the features r 322 lists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is high risk construction work (r 322)` IF
        `the work is construction work`
    AND (   `the height a person could fall, in metres` GREATER THAN 2
         OR `the depth of any trench or shaft, in metres` GREATER THAN 1.5
         OR `the work has another of the features r 322 lists`)

-- r 327(1): an employer or self-employed person "must not perform high risk construction work if there is a risk to the
-- health or safety of any person arising from the work, unless (a) a safe work method statement is prepared for the work
-- before the work commences; and (b) the work is performed in accordance with the statement"; (3): for asbestos work, an
-- asbestos control plan under r 272 counts as the statement.
GIVEN `the work is high risk construction work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a risk to anyone's health or safety from the work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a safe work method statement (or asbestos control plan) was prepared before the work began` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work was done in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 327 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the work is high risk construction work` AND `there is a risk to anyone's health or safety from the work`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a safe work method statement (or asbestos control plan) was prepared before the work began` AND `the work was done in accordance with it`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 332(1): the principal contractor's duties (signs, a health and safety co-ordination plan, its availability) apply "to
-- a construction project if the cost of the project is $350 000 or more"; r 558(1): to one costing $250 000 or more "if
-- the construction contract for the project was entered into before 1 July 2014".
GIVEN `the cost of the project in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the construction contract was entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the principal contractor's duties apply (rr 332, 558)` MEANS
    IF `the cost of the project in dollars` AT LEAST 350000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the day the construction contract was entered into` `is before` `1 July 2014` AND `the cost of the project in dollars` AT LEAST 250000
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 349: "If a person who holds a construction induction card has not performed construction work during a consecutive
-- period of 2 years, the construction induction card lapses and is no longer current at the end of that period". The
-- card is current up to and including the day 2 years after the last construction work, and lapsed after it (NOTHING
-- else about the card is encoded: r 350 and r 351 cancellations are the Authority's).
GIVEN `the person holds a construction induction card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the person did construction work` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the construction induction card is current (r 349)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person holds a construction induction card`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` (`the date` 24 `months after` `the last day the person did construction work`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- r 341(1): "an employer must not knowingly allow a person whom the employer employs to perform construction work unless
-- the person holds a current construction induction card". r 342 exemptions: (1) the first 28 days of the employment, if
-- the person did no construction work in the preceding 2 years, the employer applies and pays for the induction training
-- within those 28 days, and the employer gives direct supervision; (2) the 60 days after the person is issued a
-- construction statement of attainment; (3) a Construction Industry Basic Induction card from before 1 July 2008 and
-- construction work in the preceding 2 years; (4) recognised evidence of construction induction training issued no more
-- than 2 years ago, or with construction work in the preceding 2 years.
GIVEN `the employer knowingly lets the person do construction work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a current construction induction card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within the first 28 days of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did construction work in the preceding 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has applied and paid for induction training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer gives direct supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within 60 days after a construction statement of attainment was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a pre-1 July 2008 basic induction card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has recognised evidence of construction induction training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that evidence was issued no more than 2 years ago` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 341 was contravened` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer knowingly lets the person do construction work`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the person holds a current construction induction card`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF    (    `it is within the first 28 days of the employment`
                     AND (NOT `the person did construction work in the preceding 2 years`)
                     AND `the employer has applied and paid for induction training`
                     AND `the employer gives direct supervision`)
                 OR `it is within 60 days after a construction statement of attainment was issued`
                 OR (`the person holds a pre-1 July 2008 basic induction card` AND `the person did construction work in the preceding 2 years`)
                 OR (    `the person has recognised evidence of construction induction training`
                     AND (`that evidence was issued no more than 2 years ago` OR `the person did construction work in the preceding 2 years`))
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 354(1): Division 4 applies to a proposed construction excavation that will be large or deep enough for a person to
-- enter, or will put anyone's health or safety at risk; (2): not to a shaft or trench dug as part of building work under a
-- building permit in force; (3): not to a mine, a Water Act bore, a quarry, or an excavation for emergency work, rescue or
-- burial. r 355(1): the employer or self-employed person "must notify the Authority ... that it intends to perform
-- construction excavation work on a shaft, trench or tunnel at least 3 days before commencing that work".
-- r 5: "construction excavation" means "(a) a trench if the excavated depth is more than 15 metres; (b) a shaft if the
-- excavated depth is more than 2 metres; (c) a tunnel". The deposited "15 metres" lost its decimal point (NOTES.md finding
-- 1): r 322(g) reads "a trench or shaft if the excavated depth is more than 1·5 metres". Encoded as 1.5 metres. A trench of
-- 1.5 metres or less, or a shaft of 2 metres or less, is not a construction excavation, so Division 4 does not apply.
DECLARE `Excavation kind` IS ONE OF
    `a shaft`
    `a trench`
    `a tunnel`
    `another excavation`

GIVEN `the kind of excavation` IS AN `Excavation kind`
      `the excavated depth in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`WorkSafe must be notified of the excavation (rr 354, 355)` MEANS
    IF `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` AND (NOT (`the kind of excavation` EQUALS `a tunnel`))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF NOT `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of excavation`
                   WHEN `a trench` THEN JUST (`the excavated depth in metres` GREATER THAN 1.5)
                   WHEN `a shaft` THEN JUST (`the excavated depth in metres` GREATER THAN 2)
                   WHEN `a tunnel` THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN `another excavation` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Regulative rules`

DECLARE `OHSR party` IS ONE OF
    `the employer`
    `the worker`

DECLARE `OHSR act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Authority in writing of the lead-risk work`
    `provide a medical examination by a registered medical practitioner`
    `commence the construction excavation work`
    `wait`

-- r 195(1): an employer who identifies a lead process as reasonably likely to cause blood lead levels above the r 193
-- figures "must notify the Authority of the identification in writing within 7 days after making the identification".
-- Clock: days from the identification; the 7th day after is the last day.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `OHSR party` `OHSR act`
`r 195(1) -- notice of lead-risk work within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `notify the Authority in writing of the lead-risk work`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "r 195(1): the Authority was not notified in writing within 7 days after the lead process was identified as lead-risk work (60 penalty units for a natural person, 300 for a body corporate)"

-- r 200(1): after a removal under r 199(1)(a) or (c), or (1A)(a) or (c), "the employer must provide for the employee to
-- have a medical examination by a registered medical practitioner within 7 days after the removal". Clock: days from the
-- removal.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `OHSR party` `OHSR act`
`r 200(1) -- medical examination within 7 days after removal` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `provide a medical examination by a registered medical practitioner`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "r 200(1): no medical examination by a registered medical practitioner within 7 days after the removal from lead-risk work (an Act compliance provision: s 22(1) of the Act, 240 penalty units for a natural person, 1200 for a body corporate)"

-- r 355(1): notice "at least 3 days before commencing that work". Clock: days from the day of the notice. Work may begin
-- on the 3rd day after the notice (notice on 1 November, work on 4 November); beginning on the day of the notice or on
-- either of the next 2 days breaks the rule (NOTES.md fork).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `OHSR party` `OHSR act`
`r 355(1) -- no excavation work until 3 days after the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `commence the construction excavation work`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "r 355(1): the construction excavation work began less than 3 days after WorkSafe was notified (60 penalty units for a natural person, 300 for a body corporate)"

§§ `Penalties`

-- Each provision in scope, with the penalty it carries. "Act compliance" provisions carry the penalty of the Act section
-- named in the note (r 7): s 21 (1800 penalty units for a natural person, 9000 for a body corporate), s 22(1) (240, 1200),
-- s 26 (1800, 9000) -- restated from the Act, Version No. 045. Where a note names several sections (for example "sections
-- 21, 23 and 24"), the penalty given is the one of the section that protects an employee of the employer (s 21, or s 22(1)
-- where named) (NOTES.md fork). Provisions with their own penalty carry it.
DECLARE `Provision` IS ONE OF
    `r 18 risk control measures installed, used and maintained`
    `r 19 information about health monitoring, at the employer's expense`
    `r 20 confidentiality of health monitoring reports and copy to the person`
    `r 26-28 hazardous manual handling`
    `r 32 determining noise exposure`
